# manifest.json records the sha256 of each artifact's bytes as they sit on disk, and
# `bsc validate` recomputes those hashes from the working tree. So a checkout has to
# reproduce the committed bytes exactly. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# line endings on a Windows checkout and every artifact reads as "changed since build",
# while the same clone on Linux validates clean -- the provenance chain would hold or
# fail depending on who cloned it.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF on every platform, matching what the pipeline writes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these, and never diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.svg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.onnx binary
